1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,250
This exercise follows a fictional route
already started for

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:04,590
the assigned training unit.

3
00:00:05,019 --> 00:00:09,180
In Settings, Realtime Geolocation and
Background Geolocation are

4
00:00:09,229 --> 00:00:11,140
off for this software exercise.

5
00:00:11,479 --> 00:00:14,300
The check-ins you will see are manual
status updates.

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:18,379
They do not demonstrate physical arrival
or geofence validation.

7
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,260
Open Routes and find the Active Route
card.

8
00:00:21,649 --> 00:00:25,639
Its zero-percent progress is separate from
the saved plan listed below it.

9
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,200
Select Active Route.

10
00:00:27,689 --> 00:00:31,240
Current Step identifies Supply point A and
shows Pending.

11
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:34,489
Review the intended stop before selecting
Check In.

12
00:00:34,839 --> 00:00:39,999
The returned current step now says In
Progress, and Check Out replaces Check In.

13
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:44,089
Progress remains zero percent because the
stop is still in progress.

14
00:00:44,469 --> 00:00:48,040
In operational use, follow your
department’s arrival procedure

15
00:00:48,079 --> 00:00:51,020
and confirm you are updating the correct
assigned route.

16
00:00:51,179 --> 00:00:54,489
After the first stop’s work is finished,
select Check Out.

17
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:57,460
The progress display changes to fifty
percent.

18
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:01,649
Current Step now identifies Community
point B, with Pending

19
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:02,750
and its Check In button.

20
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,909
Check the name and state together.

21
00:01:05,199 --> 00:01:08,890
The changed current step and percentage
provide immediate feedback that the

22
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:10,720
first stop’s checkout was saved.

23
00:01:10,950 --> 00:01:15,119
For Community point B, select Check In.
The returned current

24
00:01:15,119 --> 00:01:17,220
step now says In Progress.

25
00:01:17,539 --> 00:01:20,529
Select Check Out after completing that
stop’s work.

26
00:01:20,859 --> 00:01:24,359
The page now shows one hundred percent and
Stops Completed.

27
00:01:24,739 --> 00:01:27,029
Scroll the stop list to reach End Route.

28
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:31,759
Finishing all the stop checkouts and
ending the route are separate actions; the

29
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:33,959
End Route control is still available here.

30
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:35,389
Select End Route.

31
00:01:35,869 --> 00:01:38,949
Read the confirmation asking whether you
want to end this route.

32
00:01:39,319 --> 00:01:44,319
Cancel leaves the execution open; confirm
End Route when the assignment is finished.

33
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:47,449
After confirmation, the app returns to
Routes.

34
00:01:47,729 --> 00:01:51,149
The saved Community supply loop plan
remains in the list, while

35
00:01:51,149 --> 00:01:52,729
the Active Route card is gone.

36
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:56,350
Ending this execution has not deleted the
reusable plan.

37
00:01:56,589 --> 00:02:00,610
An authorized supervisor can reopen the
same execution in Core.

38
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:05,280
Instance Info now shows Completed, unit
fifty-one thousand eight,

39
00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:09,839
a Started time, an Ended time, and
progress of two out of two.

40
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:13,750
Use these stored details to verify the
result independently

41
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,410
of the Unit screen’s navigation.

42
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:19,150
The map here is not evidence of a recorded
vehicle journey.

43
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:21,100
Scroll to Stop Timeline.

44
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:25,019
Each of the two recorded entries shows
Completed, an In

45
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:27,389
time, an Out time, and Dwell.

46
00:02:27,889 --> 00:02:31,630
These are the saved times from the manual
training check-ins and checkouts.

47
00:02:32,019 --> 00:02:36,339
Very short exercise dwell times are not
operational travel estimates.

48
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:40,929
Review these entries when investigating an
execution, while keeping your department’s

49
00:02:40,929 --> 00:02:43,310
location and reporting procedures in mind.

50
00:02:43,570 --> 00:02:46,930
Route History retains both completed
practice executions.

51
00:02:47,329 --> 00:02:50,690
Compare Started and Ended to identify the
intended run,

52
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:53,049
then use Detail to reopen it.

53
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,190
Both rows have two out of two stops
completed.

54
00:02:56,700 --> 00:03:00,479
This workflow can support community
paramedicine visits, mental health

55
00:03:00,479 --> 00:03:05,440
response logistics, search-and-rescue
supply runs, security rounds, wildland

56
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:09,700
support and industrial response teams, as
well as fire and E M S.

57
00:03:10,159 --> 00:03:14,700
Choose meaningful stops, assign the right
unit and verify saved results.

